Style the safe-area probes through the CSSOM

The probes that measure the safe-area insets are styled by setting their style
attribute, which a page whose content security policy forbids inline styles
refuses, logging an error for each probe and leaving it unstyled. Setting the
same declarations through the element's CSSOM style is not inline styling, so
such a policy lets it through.

